                <pb facs="0994" n="1952" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1952"/>

                <head>No. 78.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wurts
                        to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11, 1887</date>.
                        (Received August 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 136.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to aknowledge the receipt
                    of your circular instruction of July 9, 1887, with its inclosures, relating to
                    the proposal to remove tonnage and other charges on navigation, and to inform
                    you that I have communicated the same to the Russian minister of foreign
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George W. Wurts.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
